<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two SKorean firms seek 21,500T U.S. wheat Thursday.</title>
<headline>Two SKorean firms seek 21,500T U.S. wheat Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheiljedang Corp and Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd have invited tenders for a total of 21,500 tonnes of U.S. wheat by 2:00 p.m. (0500 GMT) on Thursday, traders said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Cheiljedang is seeking to buy 10,000 tonnes at basis over March futures on the Chicago Board of Trade, traders said. Dongah wants to buy the remaining 11,500 tonnes, but no further details were available on Dongah's purchase plan.</p>
<p>Shipment was set for January 15-February 15 to the south eastern port of Pusan, they said.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
